WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Validation starts with basic GPU detection.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.790
Confirm that the system sees the device, the driver is loaded,

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.650
and the expected management tools report useful status.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.340
Check VRAM, utilization, temperature, power, and running processes.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.990
These checks tell you whether the system recognizes the hardware and whether anything is

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.540
already consuming resources.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.920
The next step is an AI runtime smoke test.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.619
Run a simple inference task through the same path the real workload will use:

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:27.980
host Python environment, container, notebook, inference server, or API endpoint.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.590
Confirm that acceleration is active, not just that the model responds.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.880
CPU fallback can make a test appear successful while hiding the fact that the GPU is

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:36.500
unused.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.785
Performance checks should look at prompt processing speed, generation speed, memory use,

00:00:40.785 --> 00:00:42.242
temperature, power, and throttling.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.760
For vision or embedding workflows,

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.135
use task-appropriate metrics such as processing time or throughput.

00:00:47.135 --> 00:00:50.130
Compare results against expected behavior for the model and hardware.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:53.605
A sudden performance drop may indicate driver issues, thermal limits,

00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:56.290
wrong runtime settings, or an unintended fallback path.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:00.100
Distinguish driver problems from model, runtime, or configuration problems.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.360
Out-of-memory errors may come from model size or context length.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.020
Slow generation may come from CPU execution rather than driver failure.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.676
Container visibility issues may be permissions or runtime configuration.

00:01:10.676 --> 00:01:15.515
A structured validation checklist helps narrow the fault domain before reinstalling

00:01:15.515 --> 00:01:16.160
drivers unnecessarily.
